---
/**
 * What we prove.
 *
 * The credibility route. A buyer who has understood the refusal immediately asks what else it
 * catches, and the honest answer has two halves: eight classes, of which this prototype
 * implements two against a real model. Saying so is not a weakness on the page — it is the
 * same disposition the product has about unmodelled plant, applied to itself.
 */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { RULES } from '../data/rules';

const live = RULES.filter((r) => r.implemented);
const spec = RULES.filter((r) => !r.implemented);

const built = RULES.filter((rule) => rule.implemented).length;
---
<Base
  title="What we prove — Interlock"
  description="The eight classes of unsafe switching sequence Interlock checks at every step, with an example of each and what the refusal names."
  sheet="The rule set"
  sheetNo="IL-200"
>
  <section class="open open--tight">
    <div class="sheet">
      <p class="label">Sheet IL-200</p>
      <h1 class="display display--sm">Eight ways a schedule that reads correctly can still be wrong.</h1>
      <p class="sub">
        Each is checked at every step against the network as it stands at that step, not against the
        sequence as a whole. A sequence is only meaningful up to its first unsafe operation.
      </p>
      <p class="small open__note">
        {built} of the eight are implemented against a live model in this build. The rest are specified
        and not yet built, and are marked as such below — a rule set that claimed eight and shipped two
        would be making exactly the kind of undeclared assumption the product refuses to make.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="sheet">
      <nav class="contents" aria-label="On this sheet">
        <span class="contents__k">On this sheet</span>
        <a href="#rules">The eight classes</a>
        <a href="#not">What it does not do</a>
      </nav>
      <ol class="rules" id="rules">
        {live.map((rule, index) => (
          <li class="rule-row">
            <div class="rule-row__n">
              <span class="mono">{String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
              <span class:list={['chip', rule.implemented ? 'chip--on' : 'chip--off']}>
                {rule.implemented ? 'implemented' : 'specified'}
              </span>
            </div>
            <div class="rule-row__b">
              <p class="rule-row__code mono">{rule.code}</p>
              <h2 class="rule-row__t">{rule.title}</h2>
              <p class="rule-row__w">{rule.what}</p>
            </div>
            <div class="rule-row__e">
              <dl class="rule-row__d">
                <div><dt>Example</dt><dd>{rule.example}</dd></div>
                <div><dt>The refusal names</dt><dd>{rule.names}</dd></div>
              </dl>
            </div>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>

      <div class="spec">
        <div class="spec__head">
          <p class="label">Specified, not yet built</p>
          <h2 class="head spec__h">Six more, written down before they were written.</h2>
          <p class="small spec__note">
            Each has a defined refusal and a worked case; none is running against a live model in this
            build. They are set tighter than the two above because that is what they are &mdash; a
            register of intent, not a claim.
          </p>
        </div>
        <ol class="spec__list">
          {spec.map((rule, index) => (
            <li class="spec__row">
              <span class="spec__n mono">{String(index + 3).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
              <span class="spec__b">
                <span class="spec__code mono">{rule.code}</span>
                <span class="spec__t">{rule.title}</span>
                <span class="spec__ex">{rule.example}</span>
              </span>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ol>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="sheet">
      <div class="split">
        <div>
          <p class="label" id="not">What it does not do</p>
          <h2 class="head">Interlock is not a power system analysis tool.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>
            Load flow, fault level, protection grading and arc flash energy are other people's tools and
            they are good ones. Interlock takes their outputs as constraints where you give them to us —
            a rating, a limit, a maximum parallel time — and checks the sequence against them.
          </p>
          <p>
            It does not simulate the electrical behaviour of your network. It answers one question, at
            every step, exhaustively: what is connected to what, and therefore what is live.
          </p>
          <p>
            That narrowness is deliberate. A tool that claimed to model everything would have to be
            trusted about everything, and the first thing a Senior Authorised Person will do is look for
            the edge of what it knows.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .open--tight { padding-block: clamp(var(--s7), 6vw, var(--s9)) clamp(var(--s7), 5vw, var(--s8)); }
  .display--sm { font-size: clamp(1.875rem, 1.1rem + 2.4vw, 3.25rem); max-width: 20ch; }
  .display + .sub { margin-top: var(--s5); }
  .open__note { margin-top: var(--s6); max-width: 52ch; padding-top: var(--s4);
    border-top: var(--w-hair) solid var(--hair); }
  .split { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.85fr) minmax(0, 1fr); gap: var(--s8); align-items: start; }
  .label + .head { margin-top: var(--s3); }

  /* A ruled register, not eight cards. The rules are one list with a shared shape; boxing each
     one would say they are eight separate things a reader may take or leave. */
  .rules { border-top: var(--w-rule) solid var(--ink); }
  /* Three columns: the index, the rule, and what demonstrates it. Two columns left the right
     third of every row empty, which over eight rows reads as a margin nobody chose. */
  .rule-row { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 7rem minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 0.95fr);
    gap: var(--s6); padding-block: var(--s6); border-bottom: var(--w-hair) solid var(--hair); }
  .rule-row__n { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--s3); align-items: flex-start; }
  .rule-row__n .mono { font-size: 1.25rem; font-weight: 500; color: var(--ink-3); }

  .chip { font-size: var(--t-micro); font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase;
    padding: 3px 7px; border: 1px solid currentColor; }
  .chip--on { color: var(--earth); }
  .chip--off { color: var(--ink-3); }

  .rule-row__code { font-size: var(--t-micro); font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: 0.1em; color: var(--ink-3); }
  .rule-row__t { margin-top: var(--s2); font-size: 1.3125rem; max-width: 30ch; }
  .rule-row__w { margin-top: var(--s3); font-size: var(--t-small); color: var(--ink-2); max-width: 62ch; }
  .rule-row__d { margin: 0; border-top: var(--w-hair) solid var(--hair); }
  .rule-row__d > div { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 4px;
    padding-block: var(--s3); border-bottom: var(--w-hair) solid var(--hair); }
  .rule-row__d > div:last-child { border-bottom: 0; }
  .rule-row__d dt { font-size: var(--t-micro); font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-3); padding-top: 2px; }
  .rule-row__d dd { margin: 0; font-size: var(--t-small); color: var(--ink); max-width: 48ch; }
  .rule-row__e { padding-top: 22px; }

  .spec { margin-top: clamp(var(--s8), 5vw, 96px); }
  .spec__head { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1.1fr);
    gap: var(--s8); align-items: end; padding-bottom: var(--s5); }
  .spec__h { margin-top: var(--s3); }
  .spec__note { max-width: 54ch; }
  .spec__list { border-top: var(--w-rule) solid var(--ink); }
  /* Three columns and a tighter row: the register reads at a glance rather than as six more
     essays, and the change of density is what breaks the page's rhythm. */
  .spec__row { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 3rem minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: var(--s4); padding-block: var(--s4); border-bottom: var(--w-hair) solid var(--hair); }
  .spec__n { font-size: var(--t-small); color: var(--ink-3); padding-top: 2px; }
  .spec__b { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 15rem minmax(0, 1fr); gap: var(--s3) var(--s5); align-items: baseline; }
  .spec__code { grid-column: 1; font-size: var(--t-micro); font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: 0.08em; color: var(--ink-3); }
  .spec__t { grid-column: 2; font-size: var(--t-body); font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
  .spec__ex { grid-column: 2; font-size: var(--t-small); color: var(--ink-2); max-width: 68ch; }

  @media (max-width: 1100px) {
    .spec__b { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 4px; }
    .spec__code, .spec__t, .spec__ex { grid-column: 1; }
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .spec__head { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: var(--s4); }
    .spec__row { grid-template-columns: 2.25rem 1fr; gap: var(--s3); }
    .split { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: var(--s5); }
    .rule-row { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: var(--s4); padding-block: var(--s5); }
    .rule-row__e { padding-top: 0; }
    .rule-row__n { flex-direction: row; align-items: center; gap: var(--s4); }
    .rule-row__d > div { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 4px; }
  }
</style>
